Subject: limit braces nesting depth

Socket CLI 2.1.0 bundles braces 3.0.3. That release caps input length and does not cap nesting depth, so a deeply nested pattern crashes the parser. No npm release contains the depth guard.

Origin: backport, https://github.com/micromatch/braces/commit/86074c6115b23609325537588006be0c7665ebf0
CVE: CVE-2026-93687
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/SocketDev/socket-cli.git 10189f65119e5ca84bf80e95f208cae83b405a3a
Adaptation: Rebased the parse depth guard onto the pnpm patch file Socket CLI applies to braces 3.0.3. Omitted the upstream compile.js debug-log cleanup and new tests, which are not part of the bundled parser. Left the package version at 3.0.3.
Verify: cmd `corepack pnpm exec node -e 'const {createRequire}=require("module");const r=createRequire(require.resolve("micromatch"));const b=r("braces");try{b("{".repeat(101)+"x"+"}".repeat(101));process.exit(1)}catch(e){if(!(e instanceof SyntaxError))throw e}console.log("depth guard verified")'` expect "depth guard verified"

